# Task 170-001-fix Execution Plan
# P0-3: Tmux Prompt Filename TaskId-Aware Fix

## Problem
`writePromptFile` in tmux.ts uses `.prompt-${hex}.txt` pattern.
Docker backend uses `.prompt-${taskId}-${hash}.txt`.
The `_cleanupOrphanedPromptFiles` filter `file.includes('-${id}-')` was designed for Docker
and never matched tmux prompts → kill() could delete arbitrary active tmux prompts.

## Fix
1. Update `writePromptFile(projectRoot, prompt, taskId?)` to accept optional taskId
2. When taskId provided: emit `.prompt-${taskId}-${hash}.txt` (Docker parity)
3. When no taskId (auditor): emit `.prompt-${hash}.txt` (legacy, unchanged)
4. Update `spawnWorker` to pass taskId to writePromptFile (line 178)
5. Update doc comment to reflect fix (ADR-048 §Negative asymmetry resolved)

